{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Write-Through Cache.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Write-Through Cache.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"write through cache write through cache","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Write-Through Cache.md","fileName":"Write-Through Cache.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Write-Through Cache","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-21 22:12\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Cloud Messaging Caching and Operations Patterns]] [[Distributed Network Caching Monitoring and Inspection]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Messaging Caching and Operations Patterns","Distributed Network Caching Monitoring and Inspection","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf","hands-onnetworkprogrammingwithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Write-Through Cache.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Write-Through Cache.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"write through cache write through cache","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Write-Through Cache.md","fileName":"Write-Through Cache.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Write-Through Cache","heading":"Write-Through Cache","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A write-through cache places the cache service in the write path: the caller writes through it, and the service updates both its fast copy and the backing store. On a miss, the cache can retrieve data from the store and retain it. Compared with cache-aside, the cache service owns more of the coherence work, though the system must still define what happens when one of the two writes fails.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Messaging Caching and Operations Patterns","Distributed Network Caching Monitoring and Inspection","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf","hands-onnetworkprogrammingwithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"page